Z||000000||Viper'sVenom||09-22-2001||09:02 PM||||Does anyone think its possible to stick this twin turbo 350 in the fiero <A HREF="http://www.grapeaperacing.com." TARGET=_blank>www.grapeaperacing.com.</A>   And is there a tranny that could hold that much power?  I don't even think the NSX tranny that I am looking at could handle it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-23-2001||01:08 AM||||The way the turbos are mounted it looks like a packaging problem in the Fiero engine bay.<BR>V8 Archie would be the person who would know about a V8 turbo swap.<P>Design One also offers a twin turbo Northstar package. This is a very expensive swap. <P>You would probably be better off with a purpose built automatic to efficiently handle that kind of power.<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed<BR>El Paso, TX||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||09-23-2001||02:28 AM||||If you got it to fit(doubt it will) you'll definetly need a stronger transaxle...  and I don't think any transaxle will handle that much HP and torque.<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">   <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||09-23-2001||11:15 AM||||Arn't twin turbo setups mostly for making more low end power? If so low end power isn't msut of an issue with a 350. I would think one big turbo would almost be allot easier then twins on a 350, and probably more powerfull.<BR>Look at the MK4 supra guies. Allot of them are geting rid of twin setups for 1 big turbo. Inline 6's dont lack low end power either... But thats a diff topic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
